  "annotation": {
    "version": 1,
    "task": "Create git-gud: run agent reviews of a change in sandboxed clones, in three stages (blind bugs, gloss honesty, gloss-informed improvements), with Claude, Codex or Cursor as reviewer",
    "summary": "`git gud review [<commit>|<range>|wip]` builds one prompt per stage, makes a disposable clone per stage and agent (blind clones get no glosses, agent config is stripped), runs the agents in parallel and prints one markdown section each. Claude runs in its own OS sandbox, as the old git-gloss script did. Codex and Cursor run inside git-gud's own bubblewrap sandbox, probed before every run, because Cursor's own sandbox confined nothing in testing. `git gud agents` reports what's installed, logged in, and whether the probe passes.",
    "groups": [
      {
        "id": "stages",
        "intent": "Build the bugs, honesty and improve prompts",
        "necessity": "required",
        "serves": "task",
        "removal_impact": "there would be nothing to send the reviewers; the stage split the user asked for wouldn't exist",
        "hunks": [
          "h13"
        ],
        "notes": "bugs: commit message(s) and pinned diff only, no gloss; the message is the author's own statement, so the stage is blind to the gloss, not to intent. honesty: git-gloss's own review prompt, unchanged. improve: git gloss review --material plus git-gud's instructions (framing the material as untrusted), capped by --max; falls back to the diff without a gloss. A missing gloss skips honesty with a note."
      },
      {
        "id": "workspace",
        "intent": "Make a fresh repo per run holding only the target's history, agent config removed",
        "necessity": "required",
        "serves": "task",
        "removal_impact": "reviewers would run in the real repository, could be instructed by the reviewed change's CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/.cursor, and the blind stage would see glosses",
        "evidence": "Tests: the blind clone holds no note blob and no later commit (checked with cat-file --batch-all-objects; the test fails against the old git clone), nested config is found, a range's base is present.",
        "hunks": [
          "h14"
        ],
        "notes": "The repo is created with git init (no templates, so no hooks) and receives the target, and a range's base, by push, so it has only history reachable from them: no later commits, other branches or, for the blind stage, note objects. A plain local clone copied every object, which leaked the gloss into the blind clone (found by git-gud's own bugs review). Agent config (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, .claude, .cursor, .codex, GEMINI.md, copilot instructions, ...) is removed at any depth, since agents read nested files."
      },
      {
        "id": "agents",
        "intent": "Adapters that run Claude, Codex or Cursor on a prompt in a workspace",
        "necessity": "required",
        "serves": "task",
        "removal_impact": "no reviewer could be run; the pluggable-reviewer part of the task would be missing",
        "evidence": "Claude settings are the old script's. Cursor ran live inside the sandbox (home showed only its own state; a write to /var/tmp failed). runAgent's stdin, output-file and failure handling are unit-tested.",
        "hunks": [
